course: dictionary
lesson: 10455
title: Truth and true facts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A truth is something that really is so. It is a fact, not just what someone thinks or hopes. To tell the truth means to say what really happened, even when it is hard.
explain: Truth can also mean being honest. «He told Mum the truth» means he did not hide what had happened. When you tell the truth, people can trust you.
explain: Be careful with «the truth is». It introduces what is really so, as in «the truth is shy piranhas», which corrects a film that makes piranhas look fast and fierce. Ask yourself: is this what really happens, or what is shown to make it exciting?
explain: Other phrases use truth too. «The whole truth» means every part, not just some of it. «Moment of truth» means the time when something important is found out.
fact: Truth means what really happened, or what is really so.
fact: A truth is a fact or idea that is true.
fact: Truth is also the quality of being true or honest.
fact: «Tell the truth» means say what really happened.
fact: In science, we test ideas to find the truth, rather than just believing what we are told.
exercise: «He told Mum the truth.» What does the truth mean here? | *What really happened | A story from a book | A secret that must stay hidden | A guess about what might happen
exercise: What does «the whole truth» mean? | A picture on a box | A very loud shout | *Every part, not just some of it | Only the first part of a story
exercise: «...while the ingredients list tells the truth.» What does the ingredients list do? | It is an advert for the shop | It tells a joke | *It gives facts that are true | It makes the food look bigger
test: «Moment of truth» means: | The end of a long story | A kind of sweet | A short film about the sea | *The time when something important is found out
test: Which of these is a truth? | *Sloths really are slow | A cow can be stripped in seconds | Zootopia is a real place | Ice Age shows dinosaurs living today
exam: Why can hiding the truth make things worse? | *It can make the problem bigger and break trust | It makes the truth change into a lie | It makes people laugh more | It helps you win a prize
